      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockton%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Stockton was the first town in the Utah Territories to have surveyed streets, electric lights, and a telephone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockton%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally called Camp Relief, Stockton was renamed after the California town where many of the local soldiers came from.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/stockton_history.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mines on the western slopes of the Oquirrh Mountains established Stockton as a base camp for mining operations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockton%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
